     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi all,<div><br><div>RRBS data was made available to me as .txt files for each sample (n=121).</div><div>Here is the head of one sample:</div><div><br></div><div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">chrBase<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>chr<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>base<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>strand<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>coverage<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>freqC<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>freqT</font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">chr1.10470<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>chr1<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>10470<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>R<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>10<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>80<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>20</font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">chr1.10472<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>chr1<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>10472<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>R<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>10<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>80<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>20</font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">chr1.10485<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>chr1<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>10485<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>R<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>11<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>72.72<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>27.2727</font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">chr1.10490<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>chr1<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>10490<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>R<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>11<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>72.72<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>27.2727</font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">chr1.10494<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>chr1<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>10494<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>R<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>10<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>10<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>90</font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">chr1.10497<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>chr1<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>10497<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>F<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>42<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>50<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>50</font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">chr1.10498<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>chr1<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>10498<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>R<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>5<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>100<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>0</font></div><div><br></div></div><div><br></div><div>These files are of dimension nrow=1,403,528 ncol=7. When read using methRead they shrink in size to become nrow=777,707 ncol=7 with the exception of one sample nrow=939,852.</div><div>Has anyone encountered this before and does anyone have recommendation on how to avoid loosing this large number of sites?</div><div><br></div><div>Please note that these files do not contain missing data</div><div><br></div><div>Many thanks</div></div></div>"
